&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Sony Interactive Entertainment?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sony Interactive Entertainment isn’t just the Best Place to Play — it’s also the Best Place to Work. Sony Interactive Entertainment (SIE) is the company behind the PlayStation brand. As a subsidiary of Sony Group Corporation, we’re part of a proud legacy of innovation and excellence. SIE is a dynamic technology company, delivering cutting-edge hardware and network services to more than 100 million people and an entertainment leader, home to some of the most beloved and recognizable intellectual properties (IP) in the world. Our role at SIE is to create and nurture the experiences under the PlayStation brand, a name synonymous with entertainment excellence and creativity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Are you passionate about Quality Engineering and Test Automation?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a highly motivated, proactive Software Development Engineer in Test (SDET) to join our engineering team. In this role, you will partner closely with software engineers, product managers, and quality engineers to ensure the delivery of high-quality features across multiple PlayStation platforms and services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate has strong software development skills, enjoys building scalable automation frameworks, and is passionate about improving engineering quality through automation, continuous testing, and modern DevOps practices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design comprehensive test strategies, test plans, and test cases for new features and platform enhancements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review product requirements, functional specifications, and technical design documents to identify test scenarios and quality risks early in the development lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, develop, and maintain scalable automation frameworks for UI, API, integration, and end-to-end testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop automated tests to improve regression coverage and reduce manual testing efforts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute automated and manual testing across multiple platforms, devices, and environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate, reproduce, document, and verify software defects while collaborating with development teams to drive timely resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor automation pipelines, analyze test results, and continuously improve test reliability and execution efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate automated tests into CI/CD pipelines to support continuous integration and continuous delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with globally distributed engineering teams to deliver high-quality releases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to quality engineering best practices, coding standards, and automation strategy across the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in code reviews for automation frameworks and test infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide regular quality metrics, risk assessments, and project status updates to engineering leadership and stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering or a related technical field or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–5 years of experience in Software Development Engineering in Test (SDET), Quality Engineering or Test Automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programming experience in one or more languages such as &lt;strong&gt;Python, Java, JavaScript, C# or C++&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and maintaining automated test frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with UI automation tools such as &lt;strong&gt;Playwright, Selenium, Cypress, Appium or similar technologies&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience testing RESTful APIs using tools such as Postman, REST Assured or custom automation frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience testing SDKs, libraries, backend services, and native applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with modern web technologies such as &lt;strong&gt;React, Angular or Vue.js&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with &lt;strong&gt;Git&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;CI/CD&lt;/strong&gt; tools such as Jenkins, GitHub, CircleCI, Azure DevOps, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in Agile/Scrum software development environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical, debugging, and troubleshooting skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivated with the ability to work both independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience testing applications on gaming consoles, embedded systems, mobile devices, or consumer electronics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing production software or backend services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cloud technologies such as AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud Platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with containerization technologies including Docker and Kubernetes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of performance, scalability, security, and load testing methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with micro services architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with test reporting and analytics tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why Join PlayStation?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At PlayStation, quality is a shared responsibility. As an SDET, you’ll work alongside world-class engineers to build automation solutions that ensure millions of players enjoy reliable, high-quality gaming experiences. You’ll have the opportunity to influence engineering practices, improve development efficiency, and help shape the future of PlayStation technologies.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At SIE, we consider several factors when setting each role’s base pay range, including the competitive benchmarking data for the market and geographic location.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;Please note that the base pay range may vary in line with our hybrid working policy and individual base pay will be determined based on job-related factors which may include knowledge, skills, experience, and location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;In addition, this role &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;is eligible&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; for SIE’s top-tier benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, matching 401(k), paid time off, wellness program and coveted employee discounts for Sony products. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;This role also may be eligible for a bonus package.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; Click&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.playstation.com/benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; to learn more.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The estimated base pay range for this role is listed below.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$140,500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$210,700 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please note, Sony Interactive Entertainment conducts background checks at the offer stage for all new employees (which may include criminal background checks for some roles) and will need to process personal information to support these checks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please refer to our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.playstation.com/legal/careers-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;for more information about what personal information we collect, how we use it, who we share it with, and your data protection rights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sony is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All persons will receive consideration for employment without regard to gender (including gender identity, gender expression and gender reassignment), race (including colour, nationality, ethnic or national origin), religion or belief, marital or civil partnership status, disability, age, sexual orientation, pregnancy, maternity or parental status, trade union membership or membership in any other legally protected category.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We strive to create an inclusive environment, empower employees and embrace diversity. We encourage everyone to respond.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sony Interactive Entertainment is a Fair Chance employer and qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records will be considered for employment.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
